-- Canada Pension Plan Act, section 55.2 from subsection (5.2), and section 55.3 -- DIVISION OF UNADJUSTED
-- PENSIONABLE EARNINGS, AND INCAPACITY.
--
-- Sections 55 and 55.1 (piece cp3) let spouses or common-law partners, on divorce or separation, have
-- their unadjusted pensionable earnings for the years they lived together added up and divided equally.
-- Section 55.2 (its head and subsections (2) to (5.1) are in piece cp3, which also holds the base and first
-- additional divisions) says what follows. This module starts at subsection (5.2), the division of the
-- second additional earnings, and runs to subsection (11); section 55.3 lets the Minister treat an
-- application as made earlier when the applicant was incapable of making it.
--
-- Out of range, taken as plain inputs: whether there is a division under section 55.1 (piece cp3); the
-- earnings "determined in the same manner as ... section 78.2" (piece cp5); the Year's Basic Exemption
-- (s 20, piece cp1); what "prescribed manner" means for months of cohabitation and for the notification
-- (regs 46 and 78, piece cr2).

§ `Section 55.2 (from subsection 5.2) -- division of unadjusted pensionable earnings`

§§ `Subsection (5.2) -- division of second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings`

-- src:1570 | Division of second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings
-- src:1571 | (5.2) If there is a division under section 55.1, the second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for each person subject to the division for the period of cohabitation attributable to second additional contributions made under this Act, determined in the same manner as the total second additional pensionable earnings of a contributor attributable to second additional contributions made under this Act are determined in section 78.2, are to be added and then divided equally, and the second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings so divided are to be attributed to each person.
@ref Act s 55.2(5.2) (src:1570-1571)
GIVEN `the second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of one person for the period of cohabitation` IS A NUMBER
      `the second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of the other person for the period of cohabitation` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 55.2(5.2) — the second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed to each person` `the second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of one person for the period of cohabitation` `the second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of the other person for the period of cohabitation` MEANS
    -- "are to be added and then divided equally ... to be attributed to each person"
    (`the second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of one person for the period of cohabitation` PLUS `the second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of the other person for the period of cohabitation`) DIVIDED BY 2

§§ `Subsections (6), (6.1) and (6.2) -- effect of division on a year of division`

-- src:1572 | Effect of division of base unadjusted pensionable earnings
-- src:1573 | (6) If there is a division of base unadjusted pensionable earnings under section 55.1 and under a provincial pension plan, for the purposes of benefit calculation and payment under this Act, the total base unadjusted pensionable earnings of a contributor for a year of division are the aggregate of their base unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed under subsection (5) and their base unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed under a provincial pension plan.
@ref Act s 55.2(6) (src:1572-1573)
GIVEN `there is a division of base unadjusted pensionable earnings under section 55.1 and under a provincial pension plan` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the base unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed under subsection (5)` IS A NUMBER
      `the base unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 55.2(6) — the total base unadjusted pensionable earnings of a contributor for a year of division` `there is a division of base unadjusted pensionable earnings under section 55.1 and under a provincial pension plan` `the base unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed under subsection (5)` `the base unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed under a provincial pension plan` MEANS
    -- NOTHING: the subsection speaks only of a division under both; the text says nothing of a division under one.
    IF `there is a division of base unadjusted pensionable earnings under section 55.1 and under a provincial pension plan`
    THEN JUST (`the base unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed under subsection (5)` PLUS `the base unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed under a provincial pension plan`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1574 | Effect of division of first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings
-- src:1575 | (6.1) If there is a division of first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings under section 55.1 and under a provincial pension plan, for the purposes of benefit calculation and payment under this Act, the total first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of a contributor for a year of division are the aggregate of their first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed under subsection (5.1) and their first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed under a provincial pension plan.
@ref Act s 55.2(6.1) (src:1574-1575)
GIVEN `there is a division of first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings under section 55.1 and under a provincial pension plan` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed under subsection (5.1)` IS A NUMBER
      `the first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 55.2(6.1) — the total first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of a contributor for a year of division` `there is a division of first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings under section 55.1 and under a provincial pension plan` `the first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed under subsection (5.1)` `the first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed under a provincial pension plan` MEANS
    IF `there is a division of first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings under section 55.1 and under a provincial pension plan`
    THEN JUST (`the first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed under subsection (5.1)` PLUS `the first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed under a provincial pension plan`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1576 | Effect of division of second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings
-- src:1577 | (6.2) If there is a division of second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings under section 55.1 and under a provincial pension plan, for the purposes of benefit calculation and payment under this Act, the total second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of a contributor for a year of division are the aggregate of their second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed under subsection (5.2) and their second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed under a provincial pension plan.
@ref Act s 55.2(6.2) (src:1576-1577)
GIVEN `there is a division of second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings under section 55.1 and under a provincial pension plan` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed under subsection (5.2)` IS A NUMBER
      `the second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 55.2(6.2) — the total second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of a contributor for a year of division` `there is a division of second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings under section 55.1 and under a provincial pension plan` `the second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed under subsection (5.2)` `the second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed under a provincial pension plan` MEANS
    IF `there is a division of second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings under section 55.1 and under a provincial pension plan`
    THEN JUST (`the second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed under subsection (5.2)` PLUS `the second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed under a provincial pension plan`)
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Subsection (7) -- provincial pension plans`

-- src:1578 | Provincial pension plans
-- src:1579 | (7) No division of unadjusted pensionable earnings under section 55.1 is to be made for any month during which the persons subject to the division cohabited and for which either of them contributed to a provincial pension plan (and, for the purposes of this subsection, months during which the persons cohabited are to be determined in the prescribed manner), unless the unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed to the persons under the provincial pension plan are divided for that month in a manner substantially similar to that described in this section and section 55.1.
@ref Act s 55.2(7) (src:1578-1579)
GIVEN `the persons subject to the division cohabited during the month` IS A BOOLEAN
      `either of them contributed to a provincial pension plan for the month` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed under the provincial pension plan are divided for that month in a manner substantially similar to that described in this section and section 55.1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 55.2(7) — no division of unadjusted pensionable earnings is to be made for the month` `the persons subject to the division cohabited during the month` `either of them contributed to a provincial pension plan for the month` `the unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed under the provincial pension plan are divided for that month in a manner substantially similar to that described in this section and section 55.1` MEANS
    -- "months during which the persons cohabited are to be determined in the prescribed manner" (reg 78, piece cr2):
    -- the first input is that determination.
        `the persons subject to the division cohabited during the month`
    AND `either of them contributed to a provincial pension plan for the month`
    AND (NOT `the unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed under the provincial pension plan are divided for that month in a manner substantially similar to that described in this section and section 55.1`)

§§ `Subsections (8), (8.1) and (8.2) -- no division`

-- Not a provision: whether a month falls in the period before one of two persons reached 18 or after one
-- reached 70. Reaching an age goes through section 2(2): a period of months ending with the age counts the
-- month of the birthday (paragraph 2(2)(a)); a period commencing with the age starts the month after
-- (paragraph 2(2)(b)).
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      `date of birth of one person` IS A DATE
      `date of birth of the other person` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`cp4 a month is before one of the persons reached 18 or after one of them reached 70` month `date of birth of one person` `date of birth of the other person` MEANS
        `s 2(2)(a) — a month is counted in a period of months ending with a specified age` month `date of birth of one person` 18
    OR  `s 2(2)(b) — a month is counted in a period of months commencing with a specified age` month `date of birth of one person` 70
    OR  `s 2(2)(a) — a month is counted in a period of months ending with a specified age` month `date of birth of the other person` 18
    OR  `s 2(2)(b) — a month is counted in a period of months commencing with a specified age` month `date of birth of the other person` 70

-- src:1580 | No division
-- src:1581 | (8) No division of base unadjusted pensionable earnings under section 55.1 for a period of cohabitation of the persons subject to the division is to be made
-- src:1582 | (a) for a year in which the total base unadjusted pensionable earnings of the persons do not exceed twice the Year’s Basic Exemption;
-- src:1583 | (b) for the period before which one of the persons reached eighteen years of age or after which one of the persons reached seventy years of age;
-- src:1584 | (c) for the period in which one of the persons was a beneficiary of a retirement pension under this Act or under a provincial pension plan; and
-- src:1585 | (d) for any month that is excluded from the contributory period of one of the persons under this Act or a provincial pension plan by reason of disability.
@ref Act s 55.2(8) (src:1580-1585)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      `the total base unadjusted pensionable earnings of the persons for the year of the month` IS A NUMBER
      `the Year's Basic Exemption for the year of the month` IS A NUMBER
      `date of birth of one person` IS A DATE
      `date of birth of the other person` IS A DATE
      `one of the persons was a beneficiary of a retirement pension under this Act or under a provincial pension plan in the month` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the month is excluded from the contributory period of one of the persons under this Act or a provincial pension plan by reason of disability` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 55.2(8) — no division of base unadjusted pensionable earnings is to be made for the month` month `the total base unadjusted pensionable earnings of the persons for the year of the month` `the Year's Basic Exemption for the year of the month` `date of birth of one person` `date of birth of the other person` `one of the persons was a beneficiary of a retirement pension under this Act or under a provincial pension plan in the month` `the month is excluded from the contributory period of one of the persons under this Act or a provincial pension plan by reason of disability` MEANS
    -- The four paragraphs are alternatives: "no division ... is to be made (a) ...; (b) ...; (c) ...; and (d) ...".
    -- Each is tested for one month of the period of cohabitation (NOTES.md, fork register).
        (`the total base unadjusted pensionable earnings of the persons for the year of the month` AT MOST (2 TIMES `the Year's Basic Exemption for the year of the month`))
    OR  `cp4 a month is before one of the persons reached 18 or after one of them reached 70` month `date of birth of one person` `date of birth of the other person`
    OR  `one of the persons was a beneficiary of a retirement pension under this Act or under a provincial pension plan in the month`
    OR  `the month is excluded from the contributory period of one of the persons under this Act or a provincial pension plan by reason of disability`

-- src:1586 | No division of first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings
-- src:1587 | (8.1) No division of first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings under section 55.1 for a period of cohabitation of the persons subject to the division is to be made
-- src:1588 | (a) for a year in which the total first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of the persons do not exceed twice the Year’s Basic Exemption;
-- src:1589 | (b) for the period before which one of the persons reached 18 years of age or after which one of the persons reached 70 years of age; and
-- src:1590 | (c) for the period in which one of the persons was a beneficiary of a retirement pension under this Act or under a provincial pension plan.
@ref Act s 55.2(8.1) (src:1586-1590)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      `the total first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of the persons for the year of the month` IS A NUMBER
      `the Year's Basic Exemption for the year of the month` IS A NUMBER
      `date of birth of one person` IS A DATE
      `date of birth of the other person` IS A DATE
      `one of the persons was a beneficiary of a retirement pension under this Act or under a provincial pension plan in the month` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 55.2(8.1) — no division of first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings is to be made for the month` month `the total first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of the persons for the year of the month` `the Year's Basic Exemption for the year of the month` `date of birth of one person` `date of birth of the other person` `one of the persons was a beneficiary of a retirement pension under this Act or under a provincial pension plan in the month` MEANS
        (`the total first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of the persons for the year of the month` AT MOST (2 TIMES `the Year's Basic Exemption for the year of the month`))
    OR  `cp4 a month is before one of the persons reached 18 or after one of them reached 70` month `date of birth of one person` `date of birth of the other person`
    OR  `one of the persons was a beneficiary of a retirement pension under this Act or under a provincial pension plan in the month`

-- src:1591 | No division of second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings
-- src:1592 | (8.2) No division of second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings under section 55.1 for a period of cohabitation of the persons subject to the division is to be made
-- src:1593 | (a) for the period before which one of the persons reached 18 years of age or after which one of the persons reached 70 years of age; and
-- src:1594 | (b) for the period in which one of the persons was a beneficiary of a retirement pension under this Act or under a provincial pension plan.
@ref Act s 55.2(8.2) (src:1591-1594)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      `date of birth of one person` IS A DATE
      `date of birth of the other person` IS A DATE
      `one of the persons was a beneficiary of a retirement pension under this Act or under a provincial pension plan in the month` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 55.2(8.2) — no division of second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings is to be made for the month` month `date of birth of one person` `date of birth of the other person` `one of the persons was a beneficiary of a retirement pension under this Act or under a provincial pension plan in the month` MEANS
    -- There is no basic exemption test for the second additional earnings: paragraph (8.2) has two limbs only.
        `cp4 a month is before one of the persons reached 18 or after one of them reached 70` month `date of birth of one person` `date of birth of the other person`
    OR  `one of the persons was a beneficiary of a retirement pension under this Act or under a provincial pension plan in the month`

§§ `Subsections (9) and (10) -- payment of benefit, notification of division`

-- src:1595 | Payment of benefit
-- src:1596 | (9) Where there is a division under section 55.1 and a benefit is or becomes payable under this Act to or in respect of either of the persons subject to the division for a month not later than the month following the month in which the division takes place, the basic amount of the benefit shall be calculated and adjusted in accordance with section 46 and adjusted in accordance with subsection 45(2) but subject to the division, and the adjusted benefit shall be paid effective the month following the month in which the division takes place but in no case shall a benefit that was not payable in the absence of the division be paid in respect of the month in which the division takes place or any prior month.
@ref Act s 55.2(9) (src:1595-1596)
GIVEN `the month in which the division takes place` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 55.2(9) — the month from which the adjusted benefit is paid` `the month in which the division takes place` MEANS
    -- "the adjusted benefit shall be paid effective the month following the month in which the division takes place"
    `the month following the month of a date` `the month in which the division takes place`

-- src:1596 | (9) Where there is a division under section 55.1 and a benefit is or becomes payable under this Act to or in respect of either of the persons subject to the division for a month not later than the month following the month in which the division takes place, the basic amount of the benefit shall be calculated and adjusted in accordance with section 46 and adjusted in accordance with subsection 45(2) but subject to the division, and the adjusted benefit shall be paid effective the month following the month in which the division takes place but in no case shall a benefit that was not payable in the absence of the division be paid in respect of the month in which the division takes place or any prior month.
@ref Act s 55.2(9) (src:1596)
GIVEN `the month for which payment is in question` IS A DATE
      `the month in which the division takes place` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 55.2(9) — a benefit that was not payable without the division can be paid for the month` `the month for which payment is in question` `the month in which the division takes place` MEANS
    -- "in no case shall a benefit that was not payable in the absence of the division be paid in respect of the
    -- month in which the division takes place or any prior month"
    `the month of a date` `the month for which payment is in question` GREATER THAN `the month of a date` `the month in which the division takes place`

-- src:1597 | Notification of division
-- src:1598 | (10) Where there is a division under section 55.1, both persons subject to the division, or their respective estates, shall be notified in the prescribed manner.
@ref Act s 55.2(10) (src:1597-1598)
GIVEN `there is a division under section 55.1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 55.2(10) — both persons subject to the division, or their estates, must be notified` `there is a division under section 55.1` MEANS
    -- The manner of notice is "prescribed" (reg 46, piece cr2); the duty is the Minister's.
    `there is a division under section 55.1`

§ `Section 55.3 -- incapacity`

§§ `Subsection (4) and subsection (3) -- who the section covers, and what counts as a period of incapacity`

-- src:1616 | Application
-- src:1617 | (4) This section applies only to individuals who were incapacitated on or after January 1, 1991.
@ref Act s 55.3(4) (src:1616-1617)
GIVEN `the last day on which the individual was incapacitated` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 55.3(4) — this section applies to the individual` `the last day on which the individual was incapacitated` MEANS
    -- "individuals who were incapacitated on or after January 1, 1991": some day of incapacity falls on or after that day.
    `the last day on which the individual was incapacitated` AT LEAST (YMD 1991 1 1)

-- src:1614 | Period of incapacity
-- src:1615 | (3) For the purposes of subsections (1) and (2), a period of incapacity must be a continuous period except as otherwise prescribed.
@ref Act s 55.3(3) (src:1614-1615)
GIVEN `the period of incapacity is a continuous period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a regulation prescribes otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 55.3(3) — the period of incapacity counts` `the period of incapacity is a continuous period` `a regulation prescribes otherwise` MEANS
    `the period of incapacity is a continuous period` OR `a regulation prescribes otherwise`

§§ `Subsections (1) and (2) -- the month to which the Minister may deem the application made`

-- src:1604 | Incapacity
-- src:1605 | 55.3 (1) Where an application for a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings is made under subsection 55(1) or paragraph 55.1(1)(b) or (c) or the Minister receives the prescribed information referred to in paragraph 55.1(1)(a) and the Minister is satisfied, on the basis of evidence provided by or on behalf of a person subject to the division, that the person had been incapable of forming or expressing an intention to make an application or to provide the information to the Minister on the day on which the application was actually made or the information was actually received, the Minister may deem the application to have been made or the information to have been received in the first month in which a division could have taken place or in the month that the Minister considers the person’s last relevant period of incapacity to have commenced, whichever is the later.
@ref Act s 55.3(1) (src:1605)
GIVEN `the last day on which the individual was incapacitated` IS A DATE
      `the period of incapacity is a continuous period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a regulation prescribes otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied, on the basis of evidence provided by or on behalf of the person, that the person had been incapable of forming or expressing an intention to make the application or to provide the information on the day on which it was actually made or received` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the first month in which a division could have taken place` IS A DATE
      `the month that the Minister considers the person's last relevant period of incapacity to have commenced` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 55.3(1) — the month to which the Minister may deem the application made or the information received` `the last day on which the individual was incapacitated` `the period of incapacity is a continuous period` `a regulation prescribes otherwise` `the Minister is satisfied, on the basis of evidence provided by or on behalf of the person, that the person had been incapable of forming or expressing an intention to make the application or to provide the information on the day on which it was actually made or received` `the first month in which a division could have taken place` `the month that the Minister considers the person's last relevant period of incapacity to have commenced` MEANS
    -- NOTHING: the section gives the Minister no power to deem (it is a power: "may deem").
    IF   `s 55.3(4) — this section applies to the individual` `the last day on which the individual was incapacitated`
     AND `s 55.3(3) — the period of incapacity counts` `the period of incapacity is a continuous period` `a regulation prescribes otherwise`
     AND `the Minister is satisfied, on the basis of evidence provided by or on behalf of the person, that the person had been incapable of forming or expressing an intention to make the application or to provide the information on the day on which it was actually made or received`
    THEN JUST (`cp4 the later of two months` `the first month in which a division could have taken place` `the month that the Minister considers the person's last relevant period of incapacity to have commenced`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1606 | Incapacity
-- src:1607 | (2) Where an application for a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings is made under subsection 55(1) or paragraph 55.1(1)(b) or (c) or the Minister receives the prescribed information referred to in paragraph 55.1(1)(a) and the Minister is satisfied, on the basis of evidence provided by or on behalf of a person subject to the division, that
-- src:1608 | (a) the person had been incapable of forming or expressing an intention to make an application or to provide the information to the Minister before the day on which the application was actually made or the information was actually received by the Minister,
-- src:1609 | (b) the person had ceased to be so incapable before that day, and
-- src:1610 | (c) the application was actually made or the information was actually received by the Minister
-- src:1611 | (i) within the period that begins on the day on which the person had ceased to be so incapable and that comprises the same number of days, not exceeding twelve months, as in the period of incapacity, or
-- src:1612 | (ii) where the period referred to in subparagraph (i) comprises fewer than thirty days, not more than one month after the month in which the person had ceased to be so incapable,
-- src:1613 | the Minister may deem the application to have been made or the information to have been received in the first month in which a division could have taken place or in the month in which the Minister considers the person’s last relevant period of incapacity to have commenced, whichever is the later.
@ref Act s 55.3(2) (src:1607-1613)
GIVEN `the last day on which the individual was incapacitated` IS A DATE
      `the period of incapacity is a continuous period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a regulation prescribes otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied, on the basis of evidence provided by or on behalf of the person, that the person had been incapable of forming or expressing an intention to make the application or to provide the information before the day on which it was actually made or received, and had ceased to be so incapable before that day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the person ceased to be so incapable` IS A DATE
      `the number of days in the period of incapacity` IS A NUMBER
      `the day on which the application was actually made or the information actually received` IS A DATE
      `the first month in which a division could have taken place` IS A DATE
      `the month that the Minister considers the person's last relevant period of incapacity to have commenced` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 55.3(2) — the month to which the Minister may deem the application made or the information received after incapacity has ceased` `the last day on which the individual was incapacitated` `the period of incapacity is a continuous period` `a regulation prescribes otherwise` `the Minister is satisfied, on the basis of evidence provided by or on behalf of the person, that the person had been incapable of forming or expressing an intention to make the application or to provide the information before the day on which it was actually made or received, and had ceased to be so incapable before that day` `the day on which the person ceased to be so incapable` `the number of days in the period of incapacity` `the day on which the application was actually made or the information actually received` `the first month in which a division could have taken place` `the month that the Minister considers the person's last relevant period of incapacity to have commenced` MEANS
    IF   `s 55.3(4) — this section applies to the individual` `the last day on which the individual was incapacitated`
     AND `s 55.3(3) — the period of incapacity counts` `the period of incapacity is a continuous period` `a regulation prescribes otherwise`
     AND `the Minister is satisfied, on the basis of evidence provided by or on behalf of the person, that the person had been incapable of forming or expressing an intention to make the application or to provide the information before the day on which it was actually made or received, and had ceased to be so incapable before that day`
     AND `cp4 the application was made within the period after incapacity ceased` `the day on which the person ceased to be so incapable` `the number of days in the period of incapacity` `the day on which the application was actually made or the information actually received`
    THEN JUST (`cp4 the later of two months` `the first month in which a division could have taken place` `the month that the Minister considers the person's last relevant period of incapacity to have commenced`)
    ELSE NOTHING
